{"actor":"Will Dower","comment":null,"created_at":"2026-03-01T12:57:44Z","event_type":"status_changed","id":9,"issue_id":"hdf-libs-7pk","new_value":"{\"status\":\"in_progress\"}","old_value":"{\"id\":\"hdf-libs-7pk\",\"title\":\"Fix double URL-encoding of project path in GitLab fetcher\",\"description\":\"## Bug\\nWhen using `--project wdower/juice-shop` (namespace/path format), the GitLab fetcher returns 404. Numeric project IDs (`--project 1`) work fine.\\n\\n## Root Cause\\nIn `hdf-cli/internal/fetchers/gitlab.go`, line ~139-148: `url.PathEscape(f.params.ProjectID)` produces `wdower%2Fjuice-shop`, which is then assigned to `url.URL.Path`. When Go serializes the URL via `.String()`, it re-encodes the `%` to `%25`, producing `wdower%252Fjuice-shop` in the actual HTTP request. GitLab doesn't find that project ID, returns 404.\\n\\n## Fix\\nSet both `url.URL.Path` (decoded) and `url.URL.RawPath` (pre-encoded) so Go preserves the intended encoding. Or construct the URL string directly without going through `url.URL`.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] `hdf fetch gitlab --project wdower/juice-shop ...` works (namespace/path format)\\n- [ ] `hdf fetch gitlab --project 1 ...` still works (numeric ID)\\n- [ ] Test added for namespace/path project IDs with slashes\\n- [ ] Existing fetcher tests still pass\",\"status\":\"open\",\"priority\":2,\"issue_type\":\"bug\",\"owner\":\"will@dower.dev\",\"created_at\":\"2026-03-01T17:49:31Z\",\"created_by\":\"Will Dower\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-01T17:49:31Z\"}"}
{"actor":"Will Dower","comment":null,"created_at":"2026-03-01T17:58:56Z","event_type":"closed","id":10,"issue_id":"hdf-libs-7pk","new_value":"Fixed: URL double-encoding (RawPath), cross-platform glab config (adrg/xdg), hostname-with-port matching. Commit 90996ed.","old_value":""}
